{
    "word": "sachem",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "af4e29d3-6f50-39f4-8e16-7f02af2f4c57",
                "word": "sachem",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6887694b-270e-4523-aa4f-1655cace134f",
                        "entry_id": "af4e29d3-6f50-39f4-8e16-7f02af2f4c57",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "sachems"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bf837aa9-80e0-3f5d-886d-517431ec9c0e",
                        "entry_id": "af4e29d3-6f50-39f4-8e16-7f02af2f4c57",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A chief of one or several Native American tribe(s), especially of the Algonquians; a sagamore."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "08a7d7f2-6d8d-491a-a8b9-9c410f460326",
                                "sense_id": "bf837aa9-80e0-3f5d-886d-517431ec9c0e",
                                "text": "Planted with their broad ends on the deck, a circle of these slabs laced together, mutually sloped towards each other, and at the apex united in a tufted point, where the loose hairy fibres waved to and fro like the top-knot on some old Pottowottamie Sachem’s head."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dea9e74f-b845-41f1-b569-72e122a24e54",
                                "sense_id": "bf837aa9-80e0-3f5d-886d-517431ec9c0e",
                                "text": "If a sachem was too harsh, a tribesman might leave and join another tribe."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "92ecc6b2-ac2b-3871-b61c-96245e71d57e",
                        "entry_id": "af4e29d3-6f50-39f4-8e16-7f02af2f4c57",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A boss, a leader."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "historical",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "87d809fd-0bff-3154-b154-8ac9e3dfc384",
                        "entry_id": "af4e29d3-6f50-39f4-8e16-7f02af2f4c57",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An eminent member of a group, or an eminent person in society; a sagamore."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "archaic",
                            "historical",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "255d3fb6-8ea8-3036-9242-1ab680a22ea1",
                        "entry_id": "af4e29d3-6f50-39f4-8e16-7f02af2f4c57",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A high-ranking officer of the Tammany Hall political organization."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "31de2f2c-044f-43aa-84bf-206532353654",
                                "sense_id": "255d3fb6-8ea8-3036-9242-1ab680a22ea1",
                                "text": "The society elects annually thirteen sachems, which represent the original thirteen States. […] The other officers of the society are a Secretary, Treasurer, Sagamore, and Wiskinkie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5b030b66-b5f6-494a-83c2-701b217015c5",
                                "sense_id": "255d3fb6-8ea8-3036-9242-1ab680a22ea1",
                                "text": "Aboriginal titles were adopted and the head of each tribe was called a sachem. […] Its proprietor, Abraham Martling, was elected a sachem on several occasions and members of Tammany were often called Martling Men."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
